Day 32: The Promise of New Life | Saturday of the Fourth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“I am the resurrection and the life.”
Not someday.
Not eventually.
Now.

Welcome to Day 32 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you to step into the hope-filled promise of Jesus — a promise that reaches into every place that feels tired, worn, or lifeless. Resurrection is not just an event; it is a Person. And wherever Jesus is, new life is possible.

This spoken‑word devotional meets you in the places that feel like sealed tombs — dreams that faded, joy that dimmed, hope that slipped through your fingers. Jesus does not fear those places. He steps toward them, calls them by name, and speaks life into them.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why resurrection is a present promise, not just a future hope

How Jesus brings life to what feels dead or forgotten

Why Lent prepares your heart for renewal, joy, and new beginnings

A prayer for God to breathe new life within you

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, bring new life here.”

